✅ ✅ 1. What is CI/CD ?
👉 Definition:
CI/CD is a process to automate code integration, testing, and deployment

✅ CI (Continuous Integration)

Developers push code frequently ✅
Build + test automatically ✅


✅ CD (Continuous Delivery / Deployment)

Automatically deploy code ✅
Faster and reliable releases ✅


✅ ✅ 2. What is Jenkins ?
👉 Definition:
Jenkins is an automation server used to implement CI/CD pipelines

✅ Key Points:

Open-source ✅
Plugin-based ✅
Supports pipeline as code ✅
Integrates with Git, Docker, Kubernetes ✅


✅ ✅ 3. Jenkins Architecture
👉 Components:


Master (Controller)
→ manages jobs, schedules builds


Agent (Node)
→ executes jobs


Executor
→ runs builds


Plugins
→ extend functionality



👉 Flow:
Developer → Git Push → Jenkins → Build → Test → Deploy


✅ ✅ 4. Types of Jenkins Jobs

Freestyle Job ✅
Pipeline Job ✅ (most important)
Multibranch Pipeline ✅


✅ ✅ 5. What is Jenkins Pipeline ?
👉 Pipeline is a set of steps defined in code (Jenkinsfile)

✅ Types:

Declarative ✅ (recommended)
Scripted ✅


✅ ✅ ✅ 6. Jenkins Pipeline Structure
Groovypipeline {    agent any    stages {        stage('Build') {            steps {                echo "Building..."            }        }        stage('Test') {            steps {                echo "Testing..."            }        }        stage('Deploy') {            steps {                echo "Deploying..."            }        }    }}Show more lines

✅ ✅ ✅ 7. CI/CD Pipeline Flow (REAL)
1. Developer pushes code to Git ✅
2. Jenkins detects change ✅
3. Build triggered ✅
4. Run unit tests ✅
5. Build artifact (jar/docker image) ✅
6. Push to repository ✅
7. Deploy to server/k8s ✅
8. Notify (Slack/Email) ✅


✅ ✅ ✅ 8. Important Jenkins Concepts

✅ Pipeline as Code
👉 Store Jenkinsfile in Git ✅

✅ SCM Integration

GitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket ✅


✅ Triggers

Poll SCM
Webhooks ✅


✅ Workspace

Directory where job runs ✅



✅ ✅ ✅ 9. Credentials Management (VERY IMPORTANT)
👉 Secure storage for:

passwords
API keys
tokens


✅ Types:

username/password
secret text ✅


✅ Usage:
GroovywithCredentials([string(credentialsId: 'api_key', variable: 'API_KEY')]) {    sh 'echo $API_KEY'}Show more lines

✅ ✅ ✅ 10. Integration with Ansible (REAL CASE)
👉 Example:
Jenkins → triggers Ansible playbook → manages servers


✅ Jenkins step:
GroovyansiblePlaybook(    playbook: 'site.yml',    inventory: 'inventory.ini')Show more lines

✅ ✅ ✅ 11. CI/CD with Docker (REAL FLOW)
👉 Flow:
Code → Build Docker Image → Push to Registry → Deploy


✅ Example:
Groovydocker build -t app:v1 .docker push repo/app:v1Show more lines

